REMAINING: two steps, both PROVEN irreducibly human (no CLI/API exists)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. IdC SAML email attribute mapping (email -> ${user:email}) — REQUIRED because
   Pool A marks email Required=true (describe-user-pool) and Cognito requires the
   SAML assertion to carry an email claim (AWS Cognito dev guide). IdC does NOT
   send email by default (only Subject). CONSOLE-ONLY — proven 4 ways:
     a. sso-admin service model has NO saml/assertion/attribute-mapping operation.
     b. Live API: list-application-authentication-methods + list-application-grants
        return ValidationException "not supported for this action" for this app.
     c. CreateApplication/UpdateApplication PortalOptions carries only SignInOptions
        (Origin, ApplicationUrl) + Visibility — no assertion/attribute fields.
     d. Full scan of EVERY AWS service model: no IdC SAML-mapping write API anywhere.
2. Interactive SSO login (human enters IdC password) to mint the ID token and
   verify PreTokenGen claims tenantId + poolClass=internal. No API sets an IdC
   user password (identitystore has zero password ops; sso portal only issues
   AWS role creds) — cannot be scripted; needs the human at the IdC login page.

